{"name":"Autumn Fern","hex":"#507b49","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"autumn fern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of Japanese shield fern (Dryopteris erythrosora)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn_fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dryopteris erythrosora","blocks":[{"text":"Dryopteris erythrosora, the autumn fern or Japanese shield fern, is a species of fern in the family Dryopteridaceae, native to China South-Central, China Southeast, Japan, Korea, Nansei-shoto and Taiwan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Dryopteris_erythrosora2.jpg/330px-Dryopteris_erythrosora2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dryopteris_erythrosora"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg/500px-Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg/1280px-Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg/500px-Autumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"D. erythrosora 'Brilliance'","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutumn_Brilliance_Fern_close-up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/500px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/1280px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg/500px-Quebec_city%2C_Quebec%2C_Canada202205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik